WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.300
Friday the 13th, it all takes place out at Crystal Lake, that pleasant little camp where happy children of all ages go to spend a fun-filled summer.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.500
But this summer will be different.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:35.220
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.860
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.480
I'm Joe. And I'm Sam.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:43.400
And you'll notice that we specifically recorded this episode on Friday the 12th.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.080
We could not take the risk.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.000
This episode is brought to you on Friday the 12th.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.640
We will not wait till the Friday the 13th to properly record this episode.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.240
I think it's just safer. What do you guys think?

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.580
I'm just surprised that it almost lined up.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.560
Like, we really haven't done anything to allow this, but we almost got there.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.840
So I feel like it's a missed opportunity.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:07.960
I think we should have negotiated a little bit harder with the calendar people.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:08.820
The calendar people.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.580
Yeah. Try and make it happen.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.440
Yeah, we already had them move around some stuff to get Castlevania 2 on Halloween.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:23.560
Which was also, you know, last time we recorded a special, like, video game genre that happens to be on the same day as a spooky holiday.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.020
Things didn't work out so well for us, as I recall.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.600
So maybe it's for the best that we do it on Friday the 12th.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.460
Yeah, I could play Blacked Out that night.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:39.860
Friday the 12th would not be a good name for this movie series game franchise, but they did go with the aptly named Friday the 13th instead.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.040
That makes a lot more sense.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:42.360
It's supposed to be a little spooky.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.680
Friday the 13th as a franchise.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.940
Sean, what's the deal?

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.080
You like it?

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:53.560
You hate it? I haven't really watched any of them in maybe a decade.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.420
I saw Jason X first.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.180
It's an interesting one to see first.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.040
Did you just finish watching Alien and you were like, oh, I should watch Jason X?

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:09.700
No, no. It was just, you know, the one that came out when I was a kid and my dad rented it and we watched it and it was terrible.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:16.660
Then I watched the first one, maybe like when I was a teenager and it was okay.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:23.480
Like, you know, I don't really have any connection to the slasher movies of yore, but it wasn't terrible.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.600
What about you, Sam?

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:30.020
This is my first experience with any Friday the 13th medium.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.120
But you knew about the hockey man?

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.920
Yeah. Oh, yeah. I knew about that.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.280
I knew about because I think when I was little, kids would dress up as Jason for Halloween.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.440
Um. I don't know.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.320
That's about it, though. Just this.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.360
Okay. Joe, I'm going to guess that, yeah, you're the same, right?

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.360
I'm in the same camp.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.760
Haven't seen it. Obviously, I know about it.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:52.980
You know, I'm familiar with it.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.320
But, yeah, this is my first experience, which is probably not the best entry into the franchise.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.780
It's no worse than Jason X.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.580
Oh, okay. Well, that's good to know.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.040
Now, see, Sam, you are like a camp guy.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.700
You're currently making a video game all about life at camp.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.260
So, I was surprised to hear that you didn't have any association with Friday the 13th because

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.480
that's a camp scary movie, just like Sleepaway Camp is.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.200
Like, I feel like if you haven't seen either of those, you should start watching.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.300
I wasn't really a scary movie kid growing up.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.660
So, that's probably part of it.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.700
Or all of it.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.320
Um. Yeah.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.140
You said it's because, like, you're kind of a bitch or because you just don't really

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.840
like, uh, movies about a bad thing?

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.260
A little bit of A and B.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.140
Hmm. I feel like you, I feel like in the middle of your sentence you realized that that was

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.140
mean and then you, like, you, like, toned it back at the end.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.760
Like, no, no, it's a valid question.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:48.960
It's just one or the other.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.420
I don't want to say anything controversial here, but I was always interested in the Friday

00:03:54.420 --> 00:04:01.420
the 13th franchise, but I just, I don't know, something about the, uh, like, the hockey mask

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.060
and the brutality of it, I wasn't about that.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:08.540
I'm much more of, like, a scream guy where there is blood, but it's also fun and it's

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:09.420
engaging. It's classy.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.560
Classy murder movies.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.040
Uh, this one, not so much.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.820
So I actually saved myself a lot of time and I just read all the plots on Wikipedia one

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:22.500
night. Like, I spent one night, not recently, this was a long time ago, just reading what happens

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.560
at every single Friday the 13th.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.160
And they had me for the first two.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.120
And then things just went completely off the rails.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.080
Like, I don't even know what to say.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.080
I mean, I know you watch Jason X, but.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:40.340
Because I think that Jason as a, like, as the iconic entity that he is doesn't even show

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.320
up until the third one.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.540
Like, the mask doesn't, isn't really even, I think the mask.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.800
Well, he's not even in the first movie.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:47.800
What's the first one about?

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.640
The first one, it's the mom, yeah.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.980
Oh. Yeah, I mean, you know, see, Sam, now you're a little interested.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.220
I see it there. The wheels are spinning.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:02.020
Uh, you know, we need to talk about the box art for this game before we start talking

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.280
about the actual game itself.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:06.920
I don't know if you guys are familiar with the box art, if you need to pull it up as a

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:07.720
reference or something.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.720
But there's just a lot going on here.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.000
It's a game made by LJN, so you have the LJN rainbow.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.780
Then you have Jason, like, a bloody, you know, he's a bloody mess with an axe that I think

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:19.840
has some blood on it, too.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.820
And then he has a rainbow background behind him.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.220
And it's like, what's the decision here?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.780
Uh, to, to, you know, is that to kidify it a little bit?

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.440
To be like, oh, well, it's not that scary.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:35.640
Because, you know, it's a, it's a, it's still a video game, so you don't have to expect what

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.460
you see in the movies.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.020
But then they use the real Jason.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.420
I'm not quite sure what's going on here, but I thought it was a weird box art.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:47.380
Yeah, I like it. I think, uh, I think that more horror needs to, needs to go the colorful route, you know?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.920
There's too much black, black, white, and red.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.300
I want more pinks and purples.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.720
Yeah, I, I can't think of the last colorful horror movie I saw.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.400
What was it? It's not really a horror movie, but what was that one, uh, it was like a really unsettling

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.020
movie. Midsommar.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.300
It was based on a book series.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:07.260
Oh, okay. It was based on a book series as, like, uh, Annihilation.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.480
Wasn't that very colorful, but it was, like, creepy and unsettling?

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.940
I haven't seen it. Annihilation's great.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.200
I haven't seen it. You should go see that, too.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:21.480
Sam, you had a thought? Uh, no, I just like the, the neon colors, because it's not just that they're, you know, rainbow

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.520
colors, but they're really bright, and I wonder if that has anything to do with, like, you

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:26.420
know, 80s neon.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.400
That was, like, a thing.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.160
Probably. You know? It was just the way things were designed.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:34.600
What do kids like? Scary movies, video games, and neon.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:49.680
And in this survival horror game, you play as the six camp counselors, and the goal is

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.000
to find and defeat Jason Voorhees.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:55.780
Uh, one thing that they didn't mention is that you kind of have to find and kill him

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.160
three times to really get the job done.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.040
Uh, and hiding in a cabin or staying adrift in a canoe won't keep you safe.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.080
Jason can find you anywhere.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.840
He is always on the, uh, the game map.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.400
You are always on the game map.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.900
All the counselors are always live.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.720
Counselors. Wow, that's weird.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:17.320
All of the counselors are on the game map.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.600
Everything is happening live.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:24.100
So the only way to survive this summer is to challenge Jason face-to-face and destroy

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:31.560
him. That's funny that you, did you call it survival horror because you read that somewhere, or

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.380
are you describing it as a survival horror game yourself?

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:41.120
I was going to ask you as our resident survival, resident, that's funny too, as our, as our

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.140
resident evil survival horror expert, I was going to ask you what you think because I

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:47.160
don't know, I thought this game was a survival horror game.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:54.740
I think, yeah, in terms of it's, the mechanics that have sort of bubbled up from whatever they

00:07:54.740 --> 00:08:00.300
were thinking, uh, I, I guess this is the closest to a survival horror game that I can

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.780
see happening on the NES.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.400
It's got, uh, it's got, uh, resource management.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:11.620
It's got a semi-unstoppable forest trap, like, following you throughout.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:15.660
Um, so yeah, I think it's got the, the bones for it.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.900
It's funny just because it's like, it's obviously being on the NES, it's not scary in the way

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.960
a scary movie is where none of the imagery is going to scare you, but it does get kind

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:29.620
of scary in the way that, like, you're so vulnerable all the time that, like, you're

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:33.860
and you know that Jason's so powerful that, like, it can get, it gets stressful in the

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.360
way that a, that a scary movie can get.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.720
So I think that that, uh, was on their side.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:44.580
Yeah. That idea that Jason can be anywhere too is really cool and kind of reminds me of, uh,

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.580
in Resident Evil 2 with Mr.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.280
X, right? That's like a thing in the original game, at least.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.340
I don't know if the remake did it, but.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.460
Oh, very much so.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.880
Okay, cool. That he could just pop up whenever.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:09:00.640
Joe is right. If he pops up in broad daylight, Jason, it's not really that scary and especially with his

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.240
purple costume, it's a little strange.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.180
Uh, but you know, like still the idea that he is just anywhere on the map and you will

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:10.300
just happen to run into him is a really neat idea in itself.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.840
And that's kind of where I got that survival horror idea from.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.000
But Sean, you're right.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.980
This game is all about, you know, navigating and finding your way through the camp and getting

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:25.280
the various weapons you need to take down Jason and to, uh, light the fireplaces and stuff

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:28.420
like that. So, uh, you know, real quick, maybe we'll start with Sam here.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:35.080
What'd you guys think about navigation in this game and just like, you know, getting, getting

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.660
from the, you know, point A to point B in the quest of, of what you have to do with camp

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:43.420
counselors and everything. Did you find that intuitive where you kind of lost at what you had to do?

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.460
I'm interested. Uh, I think that it's a mix.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.500
I think parts of it are fairly intuitive.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:54.160
Like, you know, you go down the road and there is a path you can take.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:59.380
If you, if you pause to get your map up, you can see exactly where that path is going to

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.300
go. And I always felt like that made sense.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:05.340
Like I knew where I was going and I can plan a course for a character.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:12.320
Um, I think that when you're inside rooms, it's really annoying to move around, but not

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:19.140
prohibitively so, but it, it's just like, I don't know the turning and the walking forward

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.520
and backward and everything inside buildings, I thought felt really strange.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:28.420
Do you think that they made the right call there going to, going to that like pseudo 3d

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.680
for the inside the cabins?

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.360
Do you think they maybe should, I kind of feel like they should have just stuck with the side

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.820
scrolling POV even in the, uh, the cabin.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:43.040
I, I think either that or a top down kind of view would have been a lot better because

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:49.480
there's some things that like the notes that you have to find are not really the easiest

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:50.340
to locate.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:53.180
They're only visible from like one perspective too.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:59.220
Yeah. And you have to be like, even if it's in like the next room in the cabin that you're in,

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:02.080
you have to physically walk to that next room.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.940
And then after a second or two, it'll load in.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.760
And so I, I, I don't know.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:10.580
I, I, I think that that could have been done a little bit better.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:13.240
I agree that it didn't, it didn't work great.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:17.840
And it definitely could have been done better, but I still think that because it was, because

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:23.560
it, the rooms that you go in are so small, the cabins, there's not too, you can't really

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:28.560
get lost in there because they're small enough that I still think it was, I didn't mind it.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:34.740
I'll say because, because it did feel like, again, you wouldn't get lost in there, but

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:37.760
it did feel like you were kind of fumbling around in this, in this house where as I feel

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:42.320
like it was top down, it would feel a little too like a bare, it would feel a little too,

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:44.820
I don't know, empty.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.440
It'd feel a little too easy, I guess.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.720
Whereas this is like a little bit of tension building.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.340
Yeah, I'd say that the reason that they did this, like almost first person perspective

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:58.640
was to build tension because like, you don't know what's behind you, even though it's, it's

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:06.020
very, uh, systematically like, unless you're, once you know how the game works, you know

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.060
that there really won't ever be something behind you.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:14.740
But, uh, I think that the initial experience, there's a, there's a bit more tension as Joe

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.260
was saying from this perspective, it didn't work.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:24.040
Uh, and in terms of like, if it would feel better mechanically, I think the side scrolling,

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.820
keeping with side scrolling or doing that top down would be better.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.300
Uh, but I kind of get what they were trying to do.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:33.440
Yeah. And, and I'll, I'll be totally honest with everybody.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.020
The first time that I ran into Jason in there, I jumped.

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.560
I'm not even kidding, I jumped.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:42.540
Cause I knew how powerful he was and I did not expect to run into him so early.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.260
And I was like, oh my God, I got to fight him already.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:45.460
He was just there all of a sudden.

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:48.140
So, so it did, it did get me one time.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:49.800
Eight bars of health.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.860
He takes every single time he hits you.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:52.880
That's insane.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.500
That's like, that's, but that's great.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.760
I got it. I don't, I don't want to get like right to the Jason section now.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:02.280
Cause I kind of want to build up to that, but like Joe, that is important that he's that

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:06.060
scary, right? Like forget that the jump scare happened to you by seeing him in the room.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:10.380
You more, the jump scare really happened because you knew what you were up against.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:11.640
And I think that's important here.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:15.460
It just makes all the other enemies though, feel really weird.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:22.180
I can understand bats in a cave and maybe like, you know, some snakes out in the camp open or

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:25.840
something like that. But where did the zombies come into the plot here?

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.260
And I just, I don't know.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.720
I know that the game might be a little more, a little boring.

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:35.180
If the only thing you're really doing is exploring an empty camp and happened to bump into Jason,

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:36.380
like that could actually be kind of funny.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:39.100
You know, it's like an empty camp and you just run into each other.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:46.880
You're like, it's you. So, but I think, I think the, the zombies and the fact that they just spawn all the time

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:51.300
and the fact that you need to kill them to get new power-ups and stuff like that.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.920
Something just felt off about that.

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:59.520
When you compare that to the experience of running into Jason and fighting him, I, I felt

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.920
like I was playing two different games.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:08.180
Yeah. I, I don't know what, so basically when I read the manual before playing the game, it immediately

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:14.800
lost me. And I kind of knew what I was getting into when I saw that there would be zombies and

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:16.420
like rabid wolves.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:19.100
